WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.408
Subject–Verb Agreement

00:00:02.788 --> 00:00:06.478
Find the real subject. Ignore the words in between.

00:00:07.678 --> 00:00:08.677
How to spot it

00:00:09.077 --> 00:00:10.864
One verb in different forms

00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:13.740
Lots of words between subject and verb

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.998
It’s testing: whether the verb matches its true subject

00:00:19.198 --> 00:00:19.993
The method

00:00:20.393 --> 00:00:22.737
Step 1: Find the verb blank

00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:25.339
Ask: who or what is doing this?

00:00:25.889 --> 00:00:28.255
Step 2: Cross out the extras

00:00:28.535 --> 00:00:31.266
“Of the…” phrases and anything between commas.

00:00:31.816 --> 00:00:34.202
Step 3: One or more than one?

00:00:34.482 --> 00:00:36.132
Look at the subject that’s left.

00:00:36.682 --> 00:00:38.660
Step 4: Match the verb

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:43.562
Singular verbs usually end in -s: is, has, shows.

00:00:44.112 --> 00:00:45.221
In a few words

00:00:45.371 --> 00:00:48.310
Cross out. Find the subject. Match.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:50.332
The rules

00:00:50.732 --> 00:00:52.340
“Of” phrases don’t count

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.141
Wrong: The box of photos were stored.

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.818
Right: The box of photos was stored.

00:00:58.368 --> 00:00:59.708
A and B = plural

00:00:59.988 --> 00:01:02.712
Wrong: Heat and drought is forcing change.

00:01:02.992 --> 00:01:05.556
Right: Heat and drought are forcing change.

00:01:06.106 --> 00:01:09.227
Each, every, the number of = singular

00:01:09.507 --> 00:01:12.280
Wrong: Each of the paintings show a stage.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.212
Right: Each of the paintings shows a stage.

00:01:15.762 --> 00:01:16.952
Groups are singular

00:01:17.232 --> 00:01:19.360
Wrong: The council have voted.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.729
Right: The council has voted.

00:01:22.279 --> 00:01:25.137
Neither / nor: match the closer noun

00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:28.842
Right: Neither the director nor the actors were willing.

00:01:29.392 --> 00:01:31.021
Flip inverted sentences

00:01:31.301 --> 00:01:34.530
Right: Beneath the temple was a series of tunnels.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:36.770
Let’s try one

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:42.829
The collection of letters written by soldiers during the Civil War ______ historians a rare view

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:45.100
of daily life in military camps.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:50.804
Cross out the of phrase: of letters written by soldiers during the Civil War.

00:01:51.354 --> 00:01:56.826
What’s left? The collection. That’s one thing, so the verb must be singular.

00:01:57.376 --> 00:02:03.625
Offer, have offered, and are offering are all plural. Offers is singular. Choice C.

00:02:04.825 --> 00:02:05.820
Common traps

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.247
The nearest noun

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:10.407
The noun right before the verb is usually a decoy.

00:02:10.957 --> 00:02:12.168
Flipped sentences

00:02:12.448 --> 00:02:14.945
Sometimes the subject comes after the verb.

00:02:16.145 --> 00:02:17.953
Subject–Verb Agreement

00:02:18.233 --> 00:02:21.171
Cross out. Find the subject. Match.

00:02:21.721 --> 00:02:22.494
Spot it

00:02:22.694 --> 00:02:26.597
One verb in different forms (is / are, has / have)

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:27.854
Steps

00:02:28.054 --> 00:02:31.388
1. Find the verb: who or what is doing it?

00:02:31.668 --> 00:02:34.810
2. Cross out “of…” phrases + comma extras

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:37.313
3. One thing or more than one?

00:02:37.593 --> 00:02:41.008
4. Match the verb (singular often ends in -s)

00:02:41.558 --> 00:02:42.311
Remember

00:02:42.511 --> 00:02:44.913
“of” phrases never change the subject

00:02:45.193 --> 00:02:46.533
A and B → plural

00:02:46.813 --> 00:02:49.940
each, every, the number of → singular

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.161
team, council, group → singular

00:02:53.441 --> 00:02:56.161
neither / nor → match the closer noun

00:02:56.711 --> 00:02:57.316
Trap

00:02:57.516 --> 00:02:59.179
The noun right before the verb

00:02:59.929 --> 00:03:03.623
Pause the video now, and copy this page into your notes.
